BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Community Event] 2026 BRIDGE Cancer Equity Community Forum- – 
 “Healing Where We Are: Black Women\, Our Environments\, and the Power to
  Restore.” — Healing Where We Are: Black Women\, Our Environments\, an
 d the Power to Restore.
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261010T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261010T140000
DTSTAMP:20260920T141720Z
UID:winship-47efb3fd607b06f41851afa2@emory-seminars
DESCRIPTION:Program: Community Event\n\nSpeaker: 2026 BRIDGE Cancer Equity
  Community Forum- – “Healing Where We Are: Black Women\, Our Environme
 nts\, and the Power to Restore.”\n\nEvent type: Community Event\n\nTalk 
 title: Healing Where We Are: Black Women\, Our Environments\, and the Powe
 r to Restore.\n\nJoin us for the 2026 BRIDGE Cancer Equity Community Forum
 ! “Healing Where We Are: Black Women\, Our Environments\, and the Power 
 to Restore” Health is shaped by more than individual choices. It is infl
 uenced by the environments where we live\, work\, rest\, heal\, and connec
 t with one another. This year\, the BRIDGE Community Forum invites breast 
 cancer survivors\, patients\, caregivers\, researchers\, healthcare profes
 sionals\, advocates\, and community members to explore how the environment
 s where we live\, work\, rest\, and connect can shape our health and cance
 r outcomes. The forum will bring this community together for meaningful co
 nversations\, education\, and practical strategies focused on healing\, pr
 evention\, and restoration. Attendees will have the opportunity to learn\,
  connect\, share experiences\, and leave with information and resources th
 ey can use in their everyday lives. The 2026 BRIDGE Community Annual Forum
  will be held on Saturday\, October 10\, from 10:00 AM–2:00 PM at Emory.
  This year’s forum is designed to help community members better understa
 nd how the environments around us\, from air quality and neighborhoods to 
 stress\, sleep\, relationships\, and everyday products\, can influence hea
 lth and cancer outcomes. Participants will also learn practical\, evidence
 -based strategies they can take home and incorporate into their everyday l
 ives. You won’t want to miss this important and engaging event! See the 
 attached flyer for registration information.\n\nSource: https://apps.winsh
 ipcancer.emory.edu/admin/Event/6773/2026-bridge-cancer-equity-community-fo
 rum---healing-where-we-are-black-women-our-environments-and-the-power-to-r
 estore/
LOCATION:Claudia Nance Rollins Building Emory University 1518 Clifton Road
  NE Atlanta \, Georgia 30322
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://apps.winshipcancer.emory.edu/admin/Event/6773/2026-bridge-canc
 er-equity-community-forum---healing-where-we-are-black-women-our-environme
 nts-and-the-power-to-restore/
END:VEVENT
