BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Lectures and Training] 2027 UGA-Winship Cancer Research Summit
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20270412T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20270412T170000
DTSTAMP:20260920T141720Z
UID:winship-5b1d766c4730b57c5bc7c83d@emory-seminars
DESCRIPTION:Program: Lectures and Training\n\nSpeaker: 2027 UGA-Winship Ca
 ncer Research Summit\n\nEvent type: Lectures and Training\n\nOverview The 
 University of Georgia and Winship Cancer Institute of Emory University sha
 re a longstanding commitment to accelerating cancer prevention\, diagnosis
 \, and treatment and educating the next generation of cancer researchers. 
 The 2027 UGA-Winship Cancer Research Summit will focus on exploring the st
 rengths and synergies of the two institutions\, sharing knowledge and part
 nering for impact in the state of Georgia and beyond. Key Information When
 : Monday\, April 12\, 2027\, 8:30 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Where: University of Ge
 orgia Center for Continuing Education\, 1197 South Lumpkin Street Athens\,
  Athens\, GA 30602 Parking: Parking is available in the University’s Sou
 th Campus Parking Deck\, adjacent to the Georgia Center. Audience: Student
 s\, trainees and research faculty Questions: If you have any questions abo
 ut the poster session or registration\, please contact Amy O'Dell\, amy.wo
 jcik.odell@emory.edu Program Highlights Keynote Presentation will be annou
 nced Faculty presentations on emerging topics that span basic\, translatio
 nal\, clinical and population sciences Student/Trainee Flash Talks Poster 
 session reception featuring student and trainee research Registration Gene
 ral Attendee Registration: REGISTRATION will open mid-October 2026 REGISTR
 ATION Deadline April 5\, 2027 Registration is complimentary and includes m
 eals and refreshments. Abstract Submission/Event Registration for the post
 er session: REGISTRATION will open mid-October\, 2026 Poster Abstract Subm
 issions Deadline March 15\, 2027 Please submit your application early\, as
  there are limited opportunities available Contact Amy O'Dell with any que
 stions - amy.wojcik.odell@emory.edu Abstract Submission Information Eligib
 ility: Students and trainees associated with UGA- or Winship-affiliated in
 vestigators are encouraged to submit an abstract for poster presentation o
 r flash talk when they register. Submission Requirements: Abstracts should
  be text only (no figures or images please) and should not exceed 300 word
 s or 30 lines (A4 page size). Include the abstract title and the names and
  affiliations of each author. Poster Dimensions: Poster display boards are
  60 inches high and 60 inches wide. Make sure your poster fits within thes
 e dimensions. Symposium Flash Talk Opportunity - Following a preliminary r
 eview of submitted abstracts\, several exceptional students/trainees will 
 be selected to deliver a 5-minute flash talk during the symposium\, with a
  maximum of 3 slides. Presenters may indicate on the submission form their
  interest in being considered for this opportunity or opt to participate i
 n the poster session only. Poster Reception and Competition: The poster re
 ception and competition will be held on Monday\, April 12\, 2027\, from 3:
 00 p.m. to 5:00 p.m. Prizes: Poster Presenters are welcome to leave after 
 their poster has been judged. Prizes will be awarded to the top-scoring po
 ster presenters from each institution a few days after the competition. Ho
 tel Availability A limited number of hotel rooms have been reserved for pa
 rticipants from Emory University for the night of April 11\, 2027 (pending
  availability). To secure a room\, please contact Amy O'Dell amy.wojcik.od
 ell@emory.edu .\n\nSource: https://apps.winshipcancer.emory.edu/admin/Even
 t/6777/2027-uga-winship-cancer-research-summit/
LOCATION:Georgia Center for Continuing Education 1197 South Lumpkin Street
  Athens \, Georgia 30602
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
URL:https://apps.winshipcancer.emory.edu/admin/Event/6777/2027-uga-winship
 -cancer-research-summit/
END:VEVENT
